From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:23:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/34] surface coherent: one image traps per surface

Two textures over one IOSurface share a census surface, and each made its own
Coherent. Both tracked. find() gave a trap to the first in the list, so the
other never heard of a CPU write or read: a CPU read missed the other's finished
GPU output, and its image kept old bytes for good, as a tracked surface has no
resync clock. Closing one untracked the pages from under the other.

The second texture now stays lazy, its copies back keeping the pages. The
surface that traps tells it of each write, and open pages are held before it
reads, so a write that took no trap cannot be missed either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
